                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is locally cartesian closed (i.e., if every slice
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C/X
              is cartesian closed), then every slice
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C/X
              is also locally cartesian closed.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              The slice of a slice is a slice, i.e., for every
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to Y
              there is an equivalence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C/Y)/(f \colon X \to Y) \simeq C/X
            %p whence the statement immediately follows.
          #pres.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is locally cartesian closed (and has a terminal object), then the pullback functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times - \colon C \to C/X
              preserves both finite products and exponentials up to isomorphism.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_4 Proof
            %p
              Clearly
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ×
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times - \colon C \to C/x
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mi X
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_X \colon C/X \to C
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \colon A \to X
              be any morphism. From the pullback diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                            %mo ×
                            %mi Z
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mi ϕ
                                %mo ×
                                %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %mo ×
                            %mi Z
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi π
                                    %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi π
                                    %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo →
                              %mi ϕ
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A \times Z &amp; \stackrel{\phi \times 1}{\to} &amp; X \times Z \\
                    _\mathllap{\pi_A} \downarrow &amp; &amp; \downarrow _\mathrlap{\pi_X} \\
                    A &amp; \underset{\phi}{\to} &amp; X
                    }
            %p
              we conclude
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %msub
                        %mo ×
                        %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ×
                      %mi Z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≅
                      %mi A
                      %mo ×
                      %mi Z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \times_X (X \times Z) \cong A \times Z
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              via
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo ∘
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mi A
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ×
                      %mi Z
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \circ \pi_A \colon A \times Z \to X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C/X
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \times_X (X \times Z) \to X \times Y
            %p
              are in natural bijection with arrows in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Z
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo ∘
                        %msub
                          %mi π
                          %mi A
                        %mo ,
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \times Z \stackrel{\langle \phi \circ \pi_A, g\rangle}{\to} X \times Y
            %p
              which in turn are in natural bijection with arrows in the slice
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C/X
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo ,
                        %mover
                          %mi g
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi Y
                      %mi Z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \stackrel{\langle \phi, \tilde{g} \rangle}{\to} X \times Y^Z
            %p
              (where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi Y
                      %mi Z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde{g} \colon A \to Y^Z
              is obtained by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/currying"} currying
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Z
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \colon A \times Z \to Y
              in
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times - \colon C \to C/x
              preserves exponentials.
          .num_cor
            %h6#corollary Corollary
            %p
              For any
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to Y
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\ast \colon C/Y \to C/X
              preserves exponentials. In other words, the dependent sum functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_f
              and the dependent product functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod_f
              satisfy
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frobenius+reciprocity"} Frobenius reciprocity
          .proof
            %h6#proof_5 Proof
            %p
              This is by combining proposition
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#slicelcc"}
              and proposition
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#pres"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C/Y \to (C/Y)/(f \colon X \to Y) \simeq C/X
            %p
              is identified with the pullback functor
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi Y
                      %mo →
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\ast \colon C/Y \to C/X
          %p
            This state of affairs may be summarized in terms of the notion of
            = succeed ":" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyperdoctrine"} hyperdoctrine
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_5 Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is a category with
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+limits"} finite limits
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indexed+category"} indexed category
              (by forming
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+categories"} slice categories
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyperdoctrine"} hyperdoctrine
          %p
            For a proof of the statement in this form, see for instance (
            %a{:href => "#Freyd"}> Freyd
            ).
          %h4#RelationCartesianClosureBaseChangeInTypeTheory In type theory
          %p
            We formulate some of the above considerations in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/syntax"} syntax
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_6 Proposition
            %p Let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi ϕ
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↙
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi c
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X &amp;&amp;&amp;&amp; A
                    \\\
                    \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{\phi}}\searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow_{\mathrlap{c}}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    B
                    }
            %p
              be two
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/display+maps"} display maps
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theoretic
              identification
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi B
                    %mo =
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mi ϕ
                    %msup
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mi A
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi c
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [X,A]_{B} = \prod_\phi \phi^* \langle A \stackrel{c}{\to} B\rangle
            %p
              from prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DependentProductImpliesLocalCartesinClosure"}
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/syntax"} syntax
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo :
                    %mi B
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi Type
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mo =
                      %mi def
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi b
                    %mo :
                    %mi B
                    %mo ⊢
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo :
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    b : B \vdash X(b) \to A(b) : Type
                    \\;\;\;
                    \=_{def}
                    \\;\;\;
                    b : B \vdash \prod_{x : X(b)} A(\phi(x))
                    \\,.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              While equivalent under the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relation+between+type+theory+and+category+theory"} relation between type theory and category theory
            %p
              (collection of internal homs parameterized over
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              )
          .proof
            %h6#proof_6 Proof
            %p
              By definition, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/display+map"} display map
              on the right is expressed as the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type"} dependent type
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo :
                    %mi B
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi Type
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    b : B \vdash A(b) : Type
                    \\,,
            %p
              the pullback
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi^* \langle A \to B\rangle
              is expressed by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/substitution"} substitution
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi Type
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    x : X \vdash A(\phi(x)) : Type
            %p
              and next the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+product"} dependent product
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mi ϕ
                    %msup
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod_\phi \phi^* \langle A \to B\rangle
              by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo :
                    %mi B
                    %mo ⊢
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo :
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi Type
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    b : B  \vdash \prod_{x : X(b)} A(\phi(x)) : Type
                    \\,.
            %p
              Now on the right
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msub
                        %mo =
                        %mi def
                      %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi(x) =_{def} b
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              is equivalently the projection
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi pr
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} pr_1
              out of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              expressed as the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi b
                        %mo ,
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo :
                        %munder
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                          %mrow
                            %mi b
                            %mo :
                            %mi B
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi pr
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi b
                        %mo ,
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %msub
                          %mo =
                          %mi def
                        %mi b
                        %msub
                          %mo =
                          %mi def
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo :
                        %mi B
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\frac{(b,x) :  \sum_{b : B} X(b)}
                    { pr_1(b,x) =_{def} b =_{def} \phi(x)  : B}
                    \\,.
            %p
              Inserting this in the above expression makes it
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/definitional+equality"} definitionally equal
              to
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo :
                    %mi B
                    %mo ⊢
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo :
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi Type
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    b : B  \vdash \prod_{x : X(b)} A(b) : Type
                    \\,.
            %p
              This is now a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+product"} dependent product
              over a type that does not actually depend on the context
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type"} dependent
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+type"} function type
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo :
                    %mi B
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi Type
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    b : B \vdash X(b) \to A(b) : Type
                    \\,.
            %p
              which expresses the internal hom in the slice over
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
          %h3#internal_logic Internal logic
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+logic"} internal logic
            of locally cartesian closed categories is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extensional+type+theory"} extensional
            form of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+product"} dependent product
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Π
                    %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_f
            represents an extensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+product+type"} dependent product type
            in the internal logic.
          %h3#almost_local_cartesian_closure Almost local cartesian closure
          %p
            There are categories which are cartesian closed and not locally cartesian closed, but in which for some
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            the base change functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi y
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*: C/y \to C/x
            has a right adjoint. This includes
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Gpd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Gpd
            = succeed "es;" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+complex"} crossed complex
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            to be a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibration"} fibration
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            it is sufficient for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            to be a fibration or an opfibration.
          %h3#distributivity_of_dependent_sums_over_dependent_products Distributivity of dependent sums over dependent products
          %p
            See
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributivity+pullback"} distributivity pullback
          %h2#examples Examples
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_7 Proposition
            %p
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+topos"} sheaf topos
              is locally cartesian closed.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_7 Proof
            %p
              By
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giraud%27s+theorem"} Giraud's theorem
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullbacks"} pullbacks
              preserve
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor+theorem"} adjoint functor theorem
              this implies that for every morphism
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^* : \mathcal{C}_{/Y} \to \mathcal{C}_{/X}
              has a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod_f
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DependentProductImpliesLocalCartesinClosure"}
              this yields the local cartesian closure.
          %p
            More generally, every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasitopos"} quasitopos
            is locally cartesian closed.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exponentiable+morphism"} exponentiable morphism
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} cartesian closed category
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+functor"}> cartesian closed functor
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+cartesian+closed+functor"} locally cartesian closed functor
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+cartesian+closed+enriched+category"} locally cartesian closed enriched category
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+model+category"}> cartesian closed model category
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+cartesian+closed+model+category"} locally cartesian closed model category
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"}> cartesian closed (∞,1)-category
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+cartesian+closed+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} locally cartesian closed (∞,1)-category
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+cartesian+category"} locally cartesian category
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+regular+category"} locally regular category
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributivity+pullback"} distributivity pullback
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Conduch%C3%A9+functor"} Conduché functor
          %h2#references References
          %p A standard textbook account is around corollary A1.5.3 in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Johnstone"}> Peter Johnstone
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sketches+of+an+Elephant"} Sketches of an Elephant
          %p Another textbook account, that also includes the set-theoretic intuition:
          %ul
            %li#Awodey06
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steve+Awodey"} Steve Awodey
              sections 6 &amp; 9.7 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Category theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1093/acprof:oso/9780198568612.001.0001"} doi:10.1093/acprof:oso/9780198568612.001.0001
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://global.oup.com/ukhe/product/category-theory-9780199237180"} ISBN:9780199237180
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://englishonlineclub.com/pdf/Category%20Teory%20%5BEnglishOnlineClub.com%5D.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            The relation between local cartesian closure and base change/
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyperdoctrine"} hyperdoctrine
            structure is sometimes attributed to
          %ul
            %li#Freyd
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Freyd"}> Peter Freyd
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Aspects of topoi
          %p
            A discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+language"} internal language
            of locally cartesian closed categories is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/R.+A.+G.+Seely"}> R. A. G. Seely
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Locally cartesian closed categories and type theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.mcgill.ca/rags/LCCC/LCCC.pdf"} pdf
          %p exposition:
          %ul
            %li
              Xu Huang,
              %em Locally Cartesian Closed Categories
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2202.04543"}> arXiv:2202.04543
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marta+Bunge"}> Marta Bunge
                , and
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Susan+Niefield"} Susan Niefield
                %em Exponentiability and single universes
                J. Pure Appl. Algebra 148 (2000) 217–250.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fran%C3%A7ois+Conduch%C3%A9"}> François Conduché
                ,
                %em Au sujet de l’existence d’adjoints à droite aux foncteurs “image réciproque” dans la catégorie des catégories
                (French) C. R. Acad. Sci. Paris Sér. A-B 275 (1972), A891–A894.
            %li
              %p
                J. Howie,
                %em Pullback functors and crossed complexes
                , Cahiers Topologie Géom. Différentielle, 20 (1979) 281–296.
